{
  "title": "Essential conversation",
  "note": "Invite with 〜ませんか (\"won't you...?\") and suggest with 〜ましょう (\"let's...\"). Japanese often refuses softly: ちょっと… (\"it's a bit...\") trails off instead of saying no. Set phrases like おめでとうございます and がんばってください are used constantly; learn them whole.",
  "src": {
    "t": "IRODORI: Japanese for Life in Japan, The Japan Foundation",
    "u": "https://www.irodori.jpf.go.jp/en/"
  },
